   This song uses Drop-D tuning. Drop your low E string down two
   notes to D. From low to high: D A D G B E

   I'm transcribing this from a live show, not from the CD so it
   might not be 100% like the CD.
    Sometimes the chords sound better just played on the bottom
   3 strings. That would make D5(000xxx), F5(333xxx), E5(222xxx)
   and Eb5(111xxx). He sometimes plays them like that when he has
   the distortion on. You'll hear it, it's easy.
    I heard on the radio the other day an acoustic version of this
   song. I think it wasn't from a live show because there was no
   applause or anything. Maybe it's a B-side on the single or
   something. The intro was played differently there, with some
   cool slide. If anybody knows what I'm talking about, and knows
   how to play it, email it to me. Thanx.

   Hi. I'm adding to this file now, few weeks after I made it.
